WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.968
-Our first guest tonight

00:00:01.968 --> 00:00:03.369
is a Grammy Award-winning singer
and songwriter

00:00:03.369 --> 00:00:05.738
whose new album, "Chemistry,"
is available now.

00:00:05.738 --> 00:00:07.840
You also know her as the host
of "The Kelly Clarkson Show,"

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:09.108
which airs weekdays.

00:00:09.108 --> 00:00:10.643
Check your local listings
for times.

00:00:10.643 --> 00:00:12.645
Please welcome back to the show
our friend and now neighbor

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:14.280
Kelly Clarkson, everybody.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:16.349
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:31.030 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:32.598
Welcome back.

00:00:32.598 --> 00:00:34.367
-Oh, my God, I love your show.

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:36.468
Do you know that you all
look like Smurfs

00:00:36.468 --> 00:00:37.636
on the TV back there?

00:00:37.636 --> 00:00:38.971
Like, everything is blue.

00:00:38.971 --> 00:00:41.974
-Everything is blue?
-You're all blue in the TV --

00:00:41.974 --> 00:00:43.009
-In the dressing room --

00:00:43.009 --> 00:00:44.577
-No, right before
you enter the stage.

00:00:44.577 --> 00:00:46.346
-I see. Yeah.
-I was like, "Oh."

00:00:46.346 --> 00:00:47.847
-I've never seen myself on that,

00:00:47.847 --> 00:00:49.682
'cause when I'm back there,
I'm not on the screen.

00:00:49.682 --> 00:00:50.916
-Yeah, it would be tough.

00:00:50.916 --> 00:00:54.386
-I've tried
to run back and forth.

00:00:54.386 --> 00:00:56.289
How are you?
-While inebriated.

00:00:56.289 --> 00:00:58.191
-You are new to the building.

00:00:58.191 --> 00:00:59.792
This is your first week
of shows here.

00:00:59.792 --> 00:01:02.128
Today was your first episode.
-You have been to my show.

00:01:02.128 --> 00:01:04.130
-I was on your first episode.
What an honor.

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:05.464
-What an honor it was
to have you.

00:01:05.464 --> 00:01:07.667
You know I love you,
so it was an honor to have you.

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:09.369
-How do you like it so far,
being in 30 Rock?

00:01:09.369 --> 00:01:13.139
-I love it. I didn't really
realize the underground vibe.

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:14.640
Like, there's
so many restaurants.

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:17.677
There's, like, a whole world.
like, underneath.

00:01:17.677 --> 00:01:20.346
Like, I didn't know.
-Wait until Christmas.

00:01:20.346 --> 00:01:25.485
There's a giant tree outside
that's going to blow your mind.

00:01:25.485 --> 00:01:26.752
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:26.752 --> 00:01:28.287
-I knew that one.

00:01:28.287 --> 00:01:29.689
-And you've never
lived here before.

00:01:29.689 --> 00:01:31.057
This is your first time
living here.

00:01:31.057 --> 00:01:32.592
-It's my first time living here.
And I love it.

00:01:32.592 --> 00:01:34.727
-I think this is
the perfect time of year

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:36.161
to move to New York City.

00:01:36.161 --> 00:01:38.664
-I agree. Like, especially
for me personally, like,

00:01:38.664 --> 00:01:41.000
it helped that my kids
were like 100% into it.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.268
-Oh, that's good.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:42.268 --> 00:01:45.138
So it's helpful --
When they're happy, I'm happy.

00:01:45.138 --> 00:01:46.372
-Yeah. Right.
-Yeah.

00:01:46.372 --> 00:01:48.508
-And how do they like it so far?
-They love it.

00:01:48.508 --> 00:01:50.776
-Are they excited
for their first Halloween

00:01:50.776 --> 00:01:52.245
in New York City?
-They are.

00:01:52.245 --> 00:01:53.846
But actually, the thing
they just got excited about --

00:01:53.846 --> 00:01:57.050
They've been to a show before
but not since we've lived here.

00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:58.318
And it was a long time ago.

00:01:58.318 --> 00:02:00.153
So they saw "Lion King"
the other night.

00:02:00.153 --> 00:02:04.090
And then I saw "Lion King"
three times yesterday

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:07.159
'cause they re-enacted
the entire thing.

00:02:07.159 --> 00:02:08.228
And they're like,
"You know what?

00:02:08.228 --> 00:02:09.362
I'm gonna do it over.
I can do better."

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:10.763
And I'm like, "Oh,
we're gonna start fresh,

00:02:10.763 --> 00:02:13.166
aren't we, like, again.
Okay."

00:02:13.166 --> 00:02:15.034
-Like, "We're going to
go get our big puppets."

00:02:15.034 --> 00:02:16.702
-Okay.

00:02:16.702 --> 00:02:20.539
-My wife took our 7-year-old
to "Lion King," and he loved it.

00:02:20.539 --> 00:02:25.078
But then they got
in a cab to go back downtown,

00:02:25.078 --> 00:02:27.013
and he has a very early bedtime.

00:02:27.013 --> 00:02:28.414
-Oh, so do my kids.
-Okay.

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:30.550
-So his thing was --
-That's so we have a life.

00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:32.218
-Yeah. 100%.

00:02:32.218 --> 00:02:34.387
When people are like,
"My kids go to bed at 9:30,"

00:02:34.387 --> 00:02:36.723
I'm like, "And now why
don't you poison yourself?"

00:02:36.723 --> 00:02:39.058
-Yeah.
I'm like, "What?"

00:02:39.058 --> 00:02:40.793
-"How do you
make your life happy?"

00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:43.563
-I will totally lie about
actually the time if I'm tired

00:02:43.563 --> 00:02:45.097
and be like, "Bedtime."

00:02:45.097 --> 00:02:46.966
Or my daughter's like,
"Are you sure?"

00:02:46.966 --> 00:02:50.102
I'm like, "Totally sure.
Shut the blinds. It's fine."

00:02:50.102 --> 00:02:52.905
-This summer, I'd be like,
"It's nighttime,"

00:02:52.905 --> 00:02:54.473
and they'd pull the blinds back
and it would be like

00:02:54.473 --> 00:02:56.375
the sun would, like, blast in.

00:02:56.375 --> 00:02:57.676
-It's just weird.

00:02:57.676 --> 00:02:59.745
-So when she brought
my son home from "Lion King,"

00:02:59.745 --> 00:03:01.981
he'd never seen
Times Square at night.

00:03:01.981 --> 00:03:03.248
And so he saw "Lion King."

00:03:03.248 --> 00:03:04.583
But then he got home.
I'm like, "How was it?"

00:03:04.583 --> 00:03:08.520
He's like, "You can't believe
where we live."

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:10.957
He's like, "You have
no idea what's happening

00:03:10.957 --> 00:03:13.192
just on a light level
in the city."

00:03:13.192 --> 00:03:15.194
-That was my kids, actually.

00:03:15.194 --> 00:03:16.929
That was probably the first time
that they've been

00:03:16.929 --> 00:03:18.631
to Times Square,
like, at nighttime, yeah.

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:20.433
-It's really awesome.
-It is. It's really magical.

00:03:20.433 --> 00:03:23.336
-When your kids realize
what New York City is...

00:03:23.336 --> 00:03:25.271
-Yeah, and it keeps you busy.

00:03:25.271 --> 00:03:26.772
There's so many things
to do all the time.

00:03:26.772 --> 00:03:28.607
So, yeah.
-And now you obviously

00:03:28.607 --> 00:03:30.743
have hosted this show in L.A.,

00:03:30.743 --> 00:03:32.211
and I imagine
you're in a new studio.

00:03:32.211 --> 00:03:35.014
It's a little bit different,
but it must also feel like

00:03:35.014 --> 00:03:36.949
riding a bike
to some degree now.

00:03:36.949 --> 00:03:39.251
-Yeah, I mean, honestly,
like, from the very first --

00:03:39.251 --> 00:03:41.553
I like talking,
if you haven't noticed.

00:03:41.553 --> 00:03:43.689
So that part's very easy to me.

00:03:43.689 --> 00:03:45.525
I think the difference
for this season

00:03:45.525 --> 00:03:47.593
is I really needed
that fresh start,

00:03:47.593 --> 00:03:49.495
like, on a personal note,
just --

00:03:49.495 --> 00:03:52.432
Yeah, it's a rough few years,
and I just needed it.

00:03:52.432 --> 00:03:54.333
So I don't know
that I've done this show

00:03:54.333 --> 00:03:55.935
like this kind of happy before.

00:03:55.935 --> 00:03:57.503
-That's wonderful to hear.

00:03:57.503 --> 00:03:58.570
-So, yeah.
-It comes across.

00:03:58.570 --> 00:04:00.039
-It does, yeah.

00:04:00.039 --> 00:04:02.508
-Also, I want to give
a shout-out.

00:04:02.508 --> 00:04:04.810
You had a very novel idea
for your first show.

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:07.179
I was there, and the entire
audience was doormen.

00:04:07.179 --> 00:04:08.514
-Yes.
-New York City doormen

00:04:08.514 --> 00:04:09.849
and doorwomen.

00:04:09.849 --> 00:04:12.017
And what gave you that idea?

00:04:12.017 --> 00:04:13.986
Why did you want to honor
our doormen and -women?

00:04:13.986 --> 00:04:17.223
-Well, we're meshing
our crew now, right?

00:04:17.223 --> 00:04:18.557
'Cause we have some from L.A.,
some from New York.

00:04:18.557 --> 00:04:20.126
And, like, I think a lot of us,
we just got here

00:04:20.126 --> 00:04:21.494
and we're like,
"Wow, these are, like,

00:04:21.494 --> 00:04:23.962
essential people in your life
that you don't realize.

00:04:23.962 --> 00:04:26.265
You see every --
like, more than your family.

00:04:26.265 --> 00:04:28.201
And so -- And we were like,
"Yeah, let's do this."

00:04:28.201 --> 00:04:29.335
You know, a producer
came up with the idea,

00:04:29.335 --> 00:04:31.337
and then it was just so magical.

00:04:31.337 --> 00:04:33.205
You don't realize, like you
were talking about on my show,

00:04:33.205 --> 00:04:35.274
like, how your kids grow up
with these people.

00:04:35.274 --> 00:04:37.309
Like, you're always passing.
They're so helpful.

00:04:37.309 --> 00:04:39.678
It's like a part of your life
every day.

00:04:39.678 --> 00:04:41.280
-It's 100%.
-Yeah.

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:46.085
-You had a leg up on decorating
your dressing rooms.

00:04:46.085 --> 00:04:48.154
-Well, I'm the Wayfair lady,
as well, so...

00:04:48.154 --> 00:04:49.188
-Yes, you got that
going for you.

00:04:49.188 --> 00:04:50.623
-Yeah, I've got that
going for me.

00:04:50.623 --> 00:04:51.957
No, but I did actually.

00:04:51.957 --> 00:04:54.093
It's awesome, because anytime
we do decorate somewhere,

00:04:54.093 --> 00:04:55.294
I'm like, "Can I?"

00:04:55.294 --> 00:04:58.197
I always pull my discount
and I'm like, "Can I?"

00:04:58.197 --> 00:05:01.200
'Cause I have a new collection
'cause I love Montana so much.

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:04.837
And I actually really love the,
like, chic kind of ranch vibe.

00:05:04.837 --> 00:05:08.007
Like, that's my thing, so we
came up with a whole new thing.

00:05:08.007 --> 00:05:09.375
So you might see that backstage
at my show.

00:05:09.375 --> 00:05:11.443
-You also talked briefly
at your show beforehand

00:05:11.443 --> 00:05:13.146
that you're into fantasy
football this year, first year.

00:05:13.146 --> 00:05:14.146
-Oh, my God.

00:05:14.146 --> 00:05:15.981
How did you do
this past weekend?

00:05:15.981 --> 00:05:17.717
-Monday night decides it.

00:05:17.717 --> 00:05:19.952
So when this airs,
I will know how it went,

00:05:19.952 --> 00:05:21.019
but it doesn't look good.

00:05:21.019 --> 00:05:22.254
-It was not great for me.

00:05:22.254 --> 00:05:24.223
-But you also -- I said,
"Oh, that's so exciting.

00:05:24.223 --> 00:05:26.091
You're doing it.
Who was your first pick?"

00:05:26.091 --> 00:05:28.828
And you said a name that
made me think you're bad at it.

00:05:28.828 --> 00:05:30.562
[ Laughter ]

00:05:30.562 --> 00:05:33.098
-Here's the reason why.
Okay, now I'm into it.

00:05:33.098 --> 00:05:34.500
Now I know the players',
like, real names.

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:35.935
-So on draft day,
you admit you blew it.

00:05:35.935 --> 00:05:38.304
-But on draft day, I admit --
I didn't blow it,

00:05:38.304 --> 00:05:40.839
because I have Walker, Seattle,
and he's really good.

00:05:40.839 --> 00:05:42.308
Like, Walker III, what?
-But who'd you take first?

00:05:42.308 --> 00:05:43.976
Do you even remember who?
-I do.

00:05:43.976 --> 00:05:46.145
It was Kirk Cousins.
And here's the reason why.

00:05:46.145 --> 00:05:49.215
Hey, hey, hey, hey, hey.
He was ranked high.

00:05:49.215 --> 00:05:51.350
And then also, I met him
and I like him,

00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:54.620
and I like Cousins BBQ,
and so I was like, "Cool."

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:57.756
-I mean, those are all
terrible reasons.

00:05:57.756 --> 00:05:59.192
-No, I'm not kidding.

00:05:59.192 --> 00:06:02.929
I picked Andrews from the Ravens
because I like Julie Andrews.

00:06:02.929 --> 00:06:07.733
I picked R. Wilson
'cause Rita Wilson is awesome.

00:06:07.733 --> 00:06:09.602
This is how I picked
my team at first.

00:06:09.602 --> 00:06:12.571
But now I studied up
and I realized on NFL+,

00:06:12.571 --> 00:06:14.106
you can go back and watch.

00:06:14.106 --> 00:06:15.674
If you have the premium,
you can go back and watch games.

00:06:15.674 --> 00:06:17.977
Now I'm studying up.
Now I know players.

00:06:17.977 --> 00:06:20.212
I was talking to Erin backstage.
I'm ready for next season.

00:06:20.212 --> 00:06:21.513
-Well, I think maybe next year.

00:06:21.513 --> 00:06:23.182
I think next year
is where you start.

00:06:23.182 --> 00:06:26.285
-No, I did kill it, like,
a couple weeks so far.

00:06:26.285 --> 00:06:28.053
Just not this one.
-By the way, this really

00:06:28.053 --> 00:06:30.222
is bringing home the idea

00:06:30.222 --> 00:06:31.958
that fantasy football
is different than football

00:06:31.958 --> 00:06:33.393
if you're basically
drafting people

00:06:33.393 --> 00:06:34.793
because they remind you
of Julie Andrews

00:06:34.793 --> 00:06:37.162
and you're doing
as well as I am.

00:06:37.162 --> 00:06:39.264
-When you don't know
the people, you don't know --

00:06:39.264 --> 00:06:40.266
I'm like, "I don't know.

00:06:40.266 --> 00:06:41.600
They have a lot of points,
it says."

00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:44.703
And the projections?
Whatever. They lie.

00:06:44.703 --> 00:06:46.238
-Yeah.
-Liars.

00:06:46.238 --> 00:06:48.006
-You know what?
We finally agree on something.

00:06:48.006 --> 00:06:50.242
The projections?
-The projections are lying.

00:06:50.242 --> 00:06:51.511
-Liars.

00:06:51.511 --> 00:06:53.211
You guys, this is very exciting.

00:06:53.211 --> 00:06:54.947
Kelly Clarkson!

00:06:54.947 --> 00:06:57.917
Fifth season of
"The Kelly Clarkson Show"

00:06:57.917 --> 00:06:59.084
airs weekdays.

00:06:59.084 --> 00:07:00.219
Check your local listings.

00:07:00.219 --> 00:07:03.088
Her fantastic new album,
"Chemistry," is out now.

00:07:03.088 --> 00:07:05.191
Stick around. We'll be right
back with Erin Andrews.

